From: tebako-crypto feedstock
Subject: rnp 0.18.x: include the full EC headers for Botan 3.12

Botan 3.12 split the EC headers: <botan/ecc_key.h> (pulled in by
<botan/ecdh.h>) now only FORWARD-DECLARES Botan::EC_Group and
Botan::EC_Point — the full definitions live in <botan/ec_group.h> and
<botan/ec_point.h>. rnp 0.18.1's ec.cpp and the PQC hybrid
exdsa_ecdhkem.cpp use both classes by value/member access and fail:

    error: 'Botan::EC_Group' is an incomplete type
    error: member access into incomplete type 'const EC_Point'

Include the two headers (plus <botan/bigint.h> in the KEM file, which
used BigInt by value via the same transitive-include accident). Pure
include additions, no code change; harmless against older Botan (the
headers exist at least since 2.x). Upstream shape: rnp main carries
the same implicit dependency and will need the same fix when it moves
to Botan 3.12.
--- a/src/lib/crypto/ec.cpp
+++ b/src/lib/crypto/ec.cpp
@@ -38,6 +38,8 @@
 #include "botan_utils.hpp"
 #include "botan/bigint.h"
 #include "botan/ecdh.h"
+#include "botan/ec_group.h"
+#include "botan/ec_point.h"
 #include <cassert>
 #endif
 
--- a/src/lib/crypto/exdsa_ecdhkem.cpp
+++ b/src/lib/crypto/exdsa_ecdhkem.cpp
@@ -33,6 +33,9 @@
 #include "logging.h"
 #include "string.h"
 #include "utils.h"
+#include "botan/bigint.h"
+#include "botan/ec_group.h"
+#include "botan/ec_point.h"
 #include <cassert>
 
 ec_key_t::~ec_key_t()
